{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[E]Please don't dominate the rap Jack,
If you got nothin' new to say.
If you please, don't back up the tracks,
This train's got to run today.
I spent a little time on the [E7]mountain,
Spent a little time on the hill.
I heard some say, better run away;
[G]Others say [D]better stand [A]still.
Now [E]I don't know but I been told that
It's [G]hard to [D]run with the [A]weight of gold
[E]Other hand, I've heard it said,
It's [G]just as [D]hard with the [A]weight of lead
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Who can deny, who can deny,
It's not just a change of style.
One step done and another begun,
And I wonder how many miles.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
I spent a little time on the mountain,
Spent a little time on the hill,
I saw things getting out of hand
I guess they always will.
Well, I don't know, but I've been told
In the heat of the sun a man died of cold
Keep on comin' or stand and wait
With the sun so dark and the hour so late.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
You can't overlook the lack, Jack,
Of any other highway to ride,
It's got no signs or dividing lines,
And very few rules to guide.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
I spent a little time on the mountain,
Spent a little time on the hill,
I saw things getting out of hand
I guess they always will.
Now I don't know but I've been told
If the horse don't pull you got to carry the load.
I don't know whose back's that strong;
Maybe find out before too long.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
[E]One way or another, one way or another,
One way or another, this darkness has got to give. Repeat / fade
{end_of_verse}
